<Text>&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;Intermod Distortion vs Freq&amp;nbsp;Workspace&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;ABSTRACT&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;This workspace shows the spurious performance of intermods generated at different stages in an RF amplification chain.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Furthermore, a frequency dependent compression curve is extracted and plotted on a 3D graph.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;BACKGROUND&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;Each amplifier has frequency dependent parameters specified in a spreadsheet. These amplifiers are cascaded together in an RF chain. Each of these nonlinear devices will generate intermods. The intercepts of these devices vary with frequency. As such each will have different levels of intermod contribution to the total spurious output. A spectrum sweep can be used to view the overall spurious response to a single swept tone.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;SETUP&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;A cascade of three amplifiers was created with three frequency dependent behavioral models. High pass and&amp;nbsp;low pass filters along&amp;nbsp;with an attenuator are dispersed along the line up. This single design is used&amp;nbsp;with two different System Analyzes,&amp;nbsp;one for the spectrum sweep and the other for a compression sweep.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;ANALYSIS&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;U&gt;Output Swept Spectrum&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&amp;nbsp;- We can see the bread crumb trail of intermod and harmonic spectrum at the output due to a single swept input tone. &lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;U&gt;Compression_vs_Freq&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&amp;nbsp;- This graph is created using the &lt;STRONG&gt;3DGraphCompression&lt;/STRONG&gt; equation block.&amp;nbsp;This is a result of the&amp;nbsp;sweep that was run on&amp;nbsp;the &lt;STRONG&gt;System2&lt;/STRONG&gt; analysis that contains the&amp;nbsp;quick sweep of a compression curve.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;U&gt;DC Supply Table&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; - This is a simple table of DC power supply requirements needed for the cascaded lineup.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;EXERCISES&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;1.&amp;nbsp;Disable the filters and attenuator in the design and observe changes in the swept spectrum.&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;2. Can the spurious response on the entire system be improved by reordering the same components in the cascaded lineup?&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
